{
  "about": "What a route's status says about one of its parentRefs, as both halves read it: RouteInfo::statuses_for and verdict_of in src-tauri/src/resources/gateway.rs (the connections graph) and statusesFor / verdictOf in src/lib/route-verdict.ts (the trace, the routes list, the Gateway page, the map and the peek). The entries for a parent are those naming it by group, kind, name and namespace, narrowed to the ones echoing its sectionName when any do. Over those entries, one False decides; True only when every one says True, and then the one about the oldest generation speaks; anything else is pending. `none` is no entry at all, `undecided` entries without the condition. Parents are written short: group, kind and port are filled in by the tests.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "no controller wrote status",
      "routeNamespace": "shop",
      "parent": {
        "name": "public"
      },
      "entries": [],
      "accepted": {
        "state": "none"
      },
      "resolvedRefs": {
        "state": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "an entry about another Gateway is not this one's",
      "routeNamespace": "shop",
      "parent": {
        "name": "public"
      },
      "entries": [
        {
          "parent": {
            "name": "internal"
          },
          "controllerName": "example.com/gateway",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "type": "Accepted",
              "status": "False",
              "reason": "NotAllowedByListeners"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "accepted": {
        "state": "none"
      },
      "resolvedRefs": {
        "state": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "the same name in another namespace is another Gateway",
